<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Martand Sun Temple</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">8th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Martand Sun Temple is a ruined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> temple dedicated to Surya on a plateau near Anantnag in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kashmir">Kashmir</a> valley. It was built in the 8th century by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitaditya-muktapida">Lalitaditya Muktapida</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/karkota-dynasty">Karkota dynasty</a>, within a large colonnaded courtyard. It was destroyed in the late 14th or early 15th century, but its massive limestone ruins still dominate the valley.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/martand-sun-temple.jpg" alt="Martand Sun Temple" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Varun Shiv Kapur from New Delhi, India · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Martand_Sun_Temple_Central_shrine_(6133772365).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
